# The cases the native backend (stage 2) builds and runs: `sisu-conformance
# --native conformance/native.list` builds each with `sisu build --native`
# (the x86-64 backend written in Sisu, decision 331), runs the executable,
# and compares its standard output, standard error and exit status with the
# expectations the interpreter meets (conformance/README.md, "The native
# mode"), as `--native-cranelift` does with Cranelift's executables; a
# case that pins `sisu test` has its tests run by `sisu test --native`
# too (decision 460). One case per line; the list grows as the backend
# does (`--native-survey` names the cases outside it that would pass). A
# case marked `checked` stops with the checked memory model's report, which
# a debug build gives as the interpreter does (decisions 543, 544, 560
# and 561):
# `--native-release`, whose raw memory is unchecked, builds it and does not
# run it.
